Q: Creating a Menu with React.js A: <pre><code>A common and semantic structure for a navigation menu is:

&lt;nav&gt;
  &lt;ul className=&quot;menu&quot;&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/home&quot;&gt;Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/about&quot;&gt;About&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;/contact&quot;&gt;Contact&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/nav&gt;

Then make the parent list flexible:

.menu {
  display: flex;
  gap: 16px;
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 0;
}

Solution is A good semantic structure for a navigation menu is nav &gt; ul &gt; li &gt; a.
</code></pre>
